Summary for 0004:

1. Errors section documents `-EBADF`/`-EIO` for fd-backed blob descriptors, but only the anonymous `va` backing exists and the code returns neither. `-EBUSY`, `-E2BIG`, `-EOVERFLOW` (returned by the code) are missing, errnos for oversize `request_len`/`reply_len` are unspecified, and `read()` `EINTR` is really `-ERESTARTSYS`.
2. :doc:`/driver-api/ctlv` is referenced but created only in patch 13, so htmldocs warns across patches 4-12.
3. Structs, `0xBB` and the limits table are hand-copied from the UAPI header and will drift; the text omits wire minimums, signed-integer representation, depth-minus-one rule for declared schemas, op IDs/layouts of the root ops, and the kernel guarantee when userspace violates the blob in-flight rules.
4. The udev `SYMLINK+="accel/by-path/$env{ID_PATH}"` example relies on `ID_PATH`, which may not be set for this subsystem without `IMPORT{builtin}="path_id"` (please check); no `Documentation/ABI` entry for the uevent properties; commit log thin.
